01| tab 2 of 2
02| <CR> open  │  D digest  │  s sort  │  ]b breaking  │  m seen  │  o browser  │  O actions  │  p preview  │  ? keys
03|plu╭─────────────────────────────────GitSuite Plugins Report Keys · q / <Esc> close──────────────────────────────────╮
04|   │  <CR>      On a plugin: its detail. On a commit in the digest: its plugin's detail, cursor on the commit        │
05|! b│  <BS>      Back to the overview                                                                                 │
06|+ n│  D         Breaking digest: the breaking commits of every plugin in one list                                    │
07|↑ u│  s         Cycle the sort: breaking first, name, number of commits, time of the update                          │
08|   │  A         List the unchanged plugins too, or count them again                                                  │
09|1 u│  ]] / [[   Next / previous plugin's detail (in the overview's order)                                            │
10|~  │  ]b / [b   Next / previous breaking commit not marked as seen                                                   │
11|~  │  m         Mark the commit under the cursor as seen, or every new commit of the plugin under it; again: unmark  │
12|~  │  M         Mark every commit this view lists as seen                                                            │
13|~  │  o / K     Open in the browser: the commit, or on a plugin the compare page of its update; counts as seen       │
14|git│  go        Open the compare page of the plugin's update, also from a commit line                                │
15|Mov│  gy        Copy the URL `o` would open                                                                          │
16|~  │  y / Y     Copy the short / full hash (on a plugin: the commit its update ended on)                             │
17|~  │  L         lazygit in the plugin's clone (lazygit can change the clone; the report itself never does)           │
18|~  │  S         The clone's git status and last five commits, read only                                              │
19|~  │  C         The plugin's CHANGELOG, in the tab the report was opened from                                        │
20|~  │  Q         The breaking commits into the quickfix list, opened in the tab the report was opened from            │
21|~  │  F         Jump to a plugin or a commit by name (picker)                                                        │
22|~  │  O         Menu of the actions for the line under the cursor                                                    │
23|~  │  r         Read the clone under the cursor again (a failed one, say); for this tab only, nothing is stored      │
24|~  │  R         Build a new report (same mode), store it and show it                                                 │
25|~  │  p         Show or hide the preview (follows the cursor)                                                        │
26|~  │  q         Close the report tab; the report stays, `:Git plugins` opens it again                                │
27|~  │  ?         List every one of these keys                                                                         │
28|~  ╰─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
29|gitsuite://plugins/preview [-]
